_tmp_preview-*.html
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ---- Cloud-sync conflict copies ----
# iCloud/Dropbox append " 2", " 3" etc. when the same file is edited in two
# places. 124 of them had accumulated between 28 Apr and 22 Sep 2026, and
# `git add .` in Deploy TGI.command would have committed 113 of them — including
# six duplicate .html files that would have gone live as real URLs
# (/drops/lions-municipal-golf-course-austin 2 and five more). Duplicate content
# on a site being optimised for search, permanently in git history.
# No tracked file has " 2" in its name, so these patterns cannot catch real work.
* 2.*
* 3.*
* [0-9].* copy*
*\ copy.*
*\ copy\ [0-9].*

# ---- Scraped third-party pages ----
# Raw HTML saved while researching a post (e.g. research/apt-sims/*.html, 14 Oct
# 2026) carries whatever the source site embeds — 415 Colorado's page included its
# own Google Maps browser key, which tripped GitHub secret scanning. Keep the
# extracted JSON/images in research/, never the downloaded pages themselves.
research/**/*.html

# ---- Research source images (28 Oct 2026) ----
# Full-size brand photos downloaded while researching posts. Nothing on the site
# links to research/ (the cropped copies used on pages live in images/), but
# `git add .` was pushing them on every deploy: 21,700 files, ~1.5 GB, and the
# reason deploys had slowed down. They stay on disk; they just never ship.
research/**/*.jpg
research/**/*.jpeg
research/**/*.JPG
research/**/*.png
research/**/*.webp
research/**/*.gif
research/**/*.heic
research/**/*.HEIC
research/**/*.avif
research/**/*.tif
research/**/*.tiff
research/**/*.img
research/**/*.raw
research/**/*.orig
research/**/*.jpg?*
